# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values.
# `.env` is gitignored; `.env.example` is committed.

# --- Cloudflare account -----------------------------------------------------
# Wrangler needs an explicit account id when more than one Cloudflare account
# is authenticated on the machine.
#
#   npx wrangler whoami
#
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Cloudflare Access (the admin gate) ------------------------------------
#
# These two values enable the APPLICATION-LEVEL backstop on /admin, in addition
# to Cloudflare Access at the edge. See DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
#   ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN   your Zero Trust team domain, e.g.
#                        pulsegym.cloudflareaccess.com   (no https://)
#   ACCESS_AUD           the Access application's Audience (AUD) tag
#
# !! They must be set at BUILD time. Next.js middleware runs in the edge runtime
# !! and only sees variables that existed when the bundle was built — setting
# !! them as Worker `vars` will NOT work, and the guard will silently stay off.
#
# Leave both blank for local development. With no config the guard allows the
# request and logs a warning, because Cloudflare Access does not exist on
# localhost. To prove the guard works locally, set them to any value and visit
# /admin: you should get 403.
#
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# ACCESS_AUD=

# --- WhatsApp (module 8+) --------------------------------------------------
# NEVER commit these. For production use `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
#
# META_WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# META_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# CRON_SECRET=
